Hello!

I am one of those people who have quite some problems finding a name for
their characters, and are often unhappy about the chosen one. In order
to make things easier for me, I intend to write a script to generate a
character and choose a nice name appropriate for the race/role/gender
combination. At the moment I'm in the process of compiling lists of
predefined names, mainly via google. I intend to choose the names as
follows:

	* non-human races get special names regardless of the role.
	  I have already compiled lists for the races with the help of
	  some pen-and-paper RPG-sites.
	* human characters get their names mainly from the same origin
	  as their pantheon, as according to gods-341.txt

Baby naming sites are quite a good help for the second case, though the
lists need some manual editing. However, this scheme leaves me with a
few unhandled cases:

	* Priests, obviously, can't be handled this way. Suggestions?
	* All I get from searching for "Hyborian names" is references to
